bc7enc_rdo: include <stdint.h> in ert.h and utils.h

ert.h and utils.h use uint8_t, uint32_t and the other fixed-width types but do not include
<stdint.h>; they rely on another header bringing it in. With libstdc++ and libc++ on Linux
nothing does, and ert.cpp fails to compile ("unknown type name 'uint8_t'", ert.h:24; DENG-99
CI, Clang and GCC on Linux). The patch adds the include. No code changes.

Engine-local patch (DENG-99), applied by tools/vendor/vendor.py. Drop it when a pinned commit
has the fix.

diff --git a/ert.h b/ert.h
index d387f52..47bea00 100644
--- a/ert.h
+++ b/ert.h
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #pragma once
 
 #include <stdlib.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <math.h>
diff --git a/utils.h b/utils.h
index b806c58..481192c 100644
--- a/utils.h
+++ b/utils.h
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #include <stdlib.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <math.h>
